course: dictionary
lesson: 13686
title: Formal words for harm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to formal writing, such as rules, warnings and letters from doctors. Injurious is one of them. It means causing harm or damage. «Smoking is injurious to health» tells you that smoking does damage to your body.
explain: Use the clues around the word. Harm, damage and health are all in the sentence, so injurious must be a bad thing. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Harmful would fit, so injurious means something close to harmful.
explain: Formal writers choose injurious where you might say harmful or bad for. «The loud noise was injurious to the baby's hearing» means the noise was harmful to the baby's hearing. Swap in the everyday word to check it still makes sense.
fact: Injurious is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as a substance, an action or a habit.
fact: «Injurious» means causing harm or damage.
fact: «Injurious to health» means harmful to your body.
fact: Everyday words that mean the same are harmful and bad for.
fact: Injurious is used mostly in formal and legal writing, such as safety rules, warnings and exam texts.
exercise: «Too much sun can be injurious to your skin.» What does injurious mean here? | Causing joy | *Causing harm | Causing a long delay | Causing a loud noise
exercise: The label said the cleaning liquid was injurious if swallowed. Which everyday word means the same? | Delicious | *Harmful | Glorious | Curious
exercise: Find and copy the word that means causing harm: «Loud music can be injurious to your hearing.» | *injurious | music | loud | hearing
test: «The factory's smoke was injurious to the wildlife nearby.» What does injurious mean? | Causing a happy feeling | Bright and shiny | *Causing harm or damage | Making a rumbling noise
test: In the sentence «Sugar is injurious to your teeth», which everyday words could replace injurious? | *Harmful and bad for | Pretty and bright | Quiet and calm | Sweet and tasty
exam: Which formal word means the same as harmful? | *Injurious | Delightful | Cheerful | Ancient
